*
!private/
!public/
!.gitignore

# The Philippine address list — 86 provinces and the cities and barangays under
# them, as flat JSON. It is reference data, not anything a user uploaded, and
# the app cannot draw an address form without it.
#
# It was caught by the `*` above and therefore never deployed. On the server the
# three /ph-address endpoints answered 404 "Address data not found", the walk-in
# employer form's province dropdown filled itself from that answer, and so it
# stayed empty. Nothing said why: the fetch fails inside a promise.
#
# It belongs in the repository because `peso-deploy` is a `git pull`, so
# anything outside git has to be remembered and copied by hand to every server
# this is ever put on — and the thing that goes wrong when it is forgotten is a
# silent empty dropdown.
!/ph_address/
!/ph_address/**
